Port lt-util to libtropic 4.2.0 (OpenSSL CAL, Linux SPI HAL).

libtropic-util at cbc30f5 bundles libtropic v1.0.0 and the old hal/port/unix
layer. Build against an external libtropic 4.2.0 source tree instead
(-DLIBTROPIC_SRC), so the feed carries one libtropic.

API changes absorbed: TR01_ prefixes (curves, pairing slot index, random
length), lt_ecc_key_origin_t, LT_L3_SLOT_EMPTY, buffer-size arguments of
lt_ecc_key_read() and lt_r_mem_data_read(), session_status in the L3 state,
lt_dev_linux_spi_t, the logging macro. lt_hmac_sha256() now returns a status:
the MAC-and-Destroy code checks it and takes its cleanup path on failure.

The libtropic handle is zero-initialised and given a crypto context (lt_ctx_openssl_t):
in 4.x the application owns that context, and a NULL one crashed every chip command.

